{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/4046","id":4920122057,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU-508s8AAAABJUMayQ","html_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/4046","diff_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/4046.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/4046.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/issues/4046","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/4046/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/4046/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/issues/4046/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/statuses/84c2b2072e7cba265fc1e43f28ccd558b5a4cbfa","number":4046,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Research: the open PR3934 → PR3959 chain still uses PR3251's retracted idle-axis moves (no new κ)","user":{"login":"ChaloupeMusic","id":137220234,"node_id":"U_kgDOCC3Qig","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137220234?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic","html_url":"https://github.com/ChaloupeMusic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Change and scope\n\n**Scoped negative result (audit). No new κ, no selected-frontier change.**\n\nThe highest open κ claims, #3934 (0.0017348), #3939, #3955, #3958 and #3959 (0.0017367), take their complex root from #3934's hosted receivers and #3955's hosted frame selection. Both stack on #3251, which its author retracted on 2026-10-18 together with #3184, #3190, #3198 and #3200, after merged #3296 and #3311. No comment on the open chain records this.\n\nThis package binds #3187/#3296's exact eight-stream operator replay to the chain's literal MOVES files:\n\n- #3934 contains all 435,604 moves of the retracted #3251. #3934 and #3955 both contain #3296's port-0 witness (owner 0, axis 2^72, 14→8 and 15→10).\n- Each of #3934's 2,374 new moves (all into hosted receivers), replayed alone at its own owner and port, changes the exact operator: 2,274 configurations over 140 owner replicas, none preserved.\n- At owner replica 0, 55 of #3955's 112 ports donate only literal remainder axes. All 55 change the operator, port 0 included. The other 57 use reselected frames, and #3955 does not give the cell-to-axis map, so their operator is not defined and they are not replayed.\n\nWithout these moves the chain's complex side falls back to #3148 (0.0017297775), which then binds. The bit-side work of #3647 and #3959 is not affected, but it cannot raise κ while the complex side binds lower.\n\nNot covered: repaired or rescheduled exchanges, the 57 reselected #3955 ports, native and outer obligations. #3296's census, extended to all 740 owners in the #3251 retraction comment, already covers this class of single-axis transfers; what is new is the binding to the open chain's literal files.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nCard `independent-moment` (priority revision 6), scope **changed** (recorded in TASK.json) to the literal #3934/#3955 moves. Base `20ecf2891d80b5acf18d980b2164fb44ea7faa90`; contribution commits `465cfe98` (package) and `84c2b207` (vendored-input pins). Audited heads: #3934 `74fb4dfa`, #3955 `38aaf88c`, #3959 `babd2e36` (same MOVES blobs). Overlap: #3296/#3311 cover #3190's moves at owner 0, #3187 covers #3184's stars; the #3959 comments by Clear1nsight (#3995, #4010) cover the bit-side pooled owner map, not the complex root.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3 -B research/pr3934-pr3955-operator-replay/verify.py\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/pr3934-pr3955-operator-replay --check-only\n```\n\nStandard library, about 30 s. Prints `PASS_PR3934_PR3955_OPERATOR_REPLAY hosted_receiver_moves=2374 changed=2374 pr3955_owner0_identity_ports=55 changed=55 no_new_kappa` and requires equality with RESULT.json. Run locally on Windows: directly with Python 3.11.2, and through the registered replay with Python 3.12.10 (`PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE`, about 50 s). The metadata check passes. Hosted CI is separate.\n\nControls: the owner-0 port-0 witness reproduces #3296's RESULT.json (10 entries at 2^72); an axis outside the donor remainder and a self-move are rejected; an empty overlay preserves the operator. The scalar baseline does not test the owner index (another replica's data events also give it); this is stated in the README.\n\n**Independence:** the operator model, fill authentication and data events are #3187's, and the projection, remainders and declared rule are #3296's, imported unchanged. Only the owner-replica index is new, as in the #3251 retraction census.\n\n## Open next questions\n\n1. Does any reselected #3955 frame, with an explicit cell-to-axis map, preserve the operator? First step: state the map for one reselected port of owner 0 and replay it with this verifier.\n2. What is the best κ claim that uses no #3184–#3251-type idle-axis moves? First step: check #3945 (staged544, 0.0017306632) and #3802 (0.0017305784).\n\n## Credit\n\nNick Petalas (#3187), Matarener (#3296), 1337isnot1337 (#3311), Rohan Arun (#3184–#3251, #3934–#3959, and the all-owner retraction census), Jeremy Diviney (#3148), Gonzalo-Mier (#1252), Gareth Davidson (#1387). PR3133's notice is retained through #3187's vendor directory.\n\nWritten and run by Claude (Anthropic) via Claude Code, in a session donated by Erwan. No human or formal review is claimed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-19T11:21:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T11:21:12Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"49c7af88a41a51897b7dcc03fb98fd485162569f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"ChaloupeMusic:research/pr3934-pr3955-operator-replay","ref":"research/pr3934-pr3955-operator-replay","repo":{"id":1424847635,"node_id":"R_kgDOVO1zEw","name":"integer-mult-bounds","full_name":"ChaloupeMusic/integer-mult-bounds","owner":{"login":"ChaloupeMusic","id":137220234,"node_id":"U_kgDOCC3Qig","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137220234?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic","html_url":"https://github.com/ChaloupeMusic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChaloupeMusic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":true,"archived":false,"di